  "summary_en": "Ontario regulation establishing a pilot project for testing automated vehicles (SAE Levels 3-5 and truck platooning) on public highways. It sets Registrar approval, driver and system requirements, $5M minimum insurance, collision reporting, and record retention. It is revoked October 13, 2027.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Automated vehicles may be driven on highways only by owners approved by the Registrar for testing",
   "Owners must carry minimum $5M liability insurance ($8M for 8+ passenger vehicles)",
   "ADS must include engage/disengage, failure alerts and driver takeover or safe stop mechanisms",
   "Collisions must be reported to the Registrar within 10 days; records retained",
   "Level 4/5 vehicles may operate without a driver; truck platooning exempt from following-too-closely rules"
  ],
